# Bulk ship (git / PR)

Do **not** push or open a PR after every edit. That is noisy.

## Default while working

1. One branch per **topic** (or one session branch): `docs/…`, `fix/…`, `feature/…`, `build/…`. Never commit on `main`.
2. Edit and **commit locally** as needed.
3. **No `git push`.** **No PR URL.** **No `gh pr create`.**

## When the user ships

| User says | Agent does |
| --- | --- |
| **`push`** | `git push -u origin HEAD` only. Report the remote branch. Do not open a PR unless they also asked. |
| **`PR`** / **`ship`** / **`bulk ship`** | Push if needed, then open **one** PR for all commits on this branch since `main` (prefer `gh pr create` when `gh` is on PATH and authenticated; otherwise the GitHub “Compare & pull request” / `pull/new/<branch>` link). Return the PR URL. |

`bulk ship` means the same as `ship`: one push + one PR covering the whole branch, not one PR per commit.

## Do not

- Create a new branch for every tiny follow-up on the same topic — keep committing on the open topic branch.
- Squash-merge or delete remote branches unless the user asks.
- Treat **`go`** (plan approval) as permission to push or open a PR.
